  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "Prior to the commencement of development, an Energy Statement incorporating 'as-designed' Standard Assessment Procedure (SAP) outputs must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing which demonstrates how the proposed development will apply the Mayor's energy hierarchy (use less energy, supply energy efficiently and use renewable energy) to deliver at least a 35% reduction in regulated carbon dioxide (CO2) emissions compared to the Part L baseline and deliver at least a 10% reduction in total emissions (regulated and unregulated) through on-site renewable energy generation. \r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "Prior to occupation, 'as-built' Standard Assessment Procedure (SAP) outputs must be submitted to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing to demonstrate that the energy strategy has been implemented in accordance with the approved Energy Statement. All of the approved measures must thereafter be retained for as long as the development is in existence. \r\rReason: To comply with Policy 31 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The premises shall operate strictly in accordance with the submitted Management and Operational Statement (by Next Chapter Housing Ltd), including staffing rotas, shift changeover procedures, and visitor arrangements, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To protect the amenities of the occupants of neighbouring residential properties and to ensure highway safety in accordance with Policies 29 and 36 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Fire Safety Compliance Statement.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.",
    "Prior to first occupation of the development, full details of the secure cycle storage and refuse storage facilities shall be submitted to, and approved in writing by, the Local Planning Authority which shall show their positioning within the site, the size and materials of the enclosure and the means of access. The approved details shall be implemented on site prior to the first occupation of the development hereby approved and thereafter permanently retained in accordance with the approved details.\r\rReason: To ensure compliance with Policies 28, 36 and 37 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
  ],
